   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Giving opinions and agreeing",
     "texto": [
      "To give your opinion use **creo que**, **pienso que**, **me parece que**, **para mí** or **en mi opinión**. If the opinion is affirmative, the verb is **indicative**: **Creo que es** caro. If you negate it, the verb is **subjunctive**: **No creo que sea** caro.\n\n**Parecer** works like **gustar**: **me parece** caro, **me parecen** caros.\n\nTo ask for an opinion: **¿Qué te parece?** **¿Tú qué crees?**\n\nTo agree: **estoy de acuerdo**, **tienes razón**, **por supuesto**. To disagree: **no estoy de acuerdo**, **yo creo que no**, **¡qué va!**. And in between: **depende**, **puede ser**.\n\nWatch the verbs: **estar** de acuerdo and **tener** razón."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Affirmative and negative opinion",
     "texto": [
      "After an affirmative opinion comes the **indicative**; after a negative one, the **subjunctive**:\n\n- **Creo que** es buena idea.\n- **No creo que** sea buena idea.\n- **Me parece que** tienes razón.\n- **No me parece que** tengas razón.\n\nThe verb **parecer** also links to an adjective and agrees with what is being judged: **me parece** caro, **me parecen** caros. The subjunctive of **ser** is **sea, seas, sea, seamos, seáis, sean**."
     ],
